  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "Second-hand sales have finally slowed down as we approach the middle of the summer \nholidays period, having recorded just 4 deals this week comprising 1 post-Panamax, 1 Kamsarmax & 2 \nSupramax bulk carriers. We have also gathered from market insights that: \n  \nM/V ROYAL HOPE (81,011 dwt, blt 2015 JMU/Japan, NK ss due 05/2030 dd due 05/2028, 7 ho/7 \nha, B&W 6S60ME-C) - vsl is under negos in the region of $ 31 mill. \nNote: Eco, fitted with energy saving devices, energy saving hull coating & large diameter-slow speed \npropeller. \n \nM/V POLYNESIA QUEEN (82,177 dwt, blt 2012 Tsuneishi Zhoushan/China, NK ss/dd due 05/2027, \n7 ho/7 ha, B&W 6S60MC-C) - vsl is under off-market negos in the region of low-mid $ 20 mill. \n \nM/V WOOYANG BELOS (63,590 dwt, blt 2016 Shin Kasado/Japan, KR ss/dd due 04/2026, 5 ho/5 \nha, 4 x 30.7t CR, B&W 6S50ME-B9) - vsl is under off-market negos in the region of $ 30 mill, note:  \ngrain clean. \n \nM/V BLUE AKIHABARA (61,630 dwt, blt 2014 NACKS/China, NK ss due 03/2029 dd due 03/2027, \n5 ho/5 ha, 4 x 30t CR, B&W 6S50ME-B9) - vsl is under off-market negos in the region of excess $ 25 \nmill. \n \nFor a detailed review and additional information regarding these transactions, kindly refer to our \n\"representative sales\" section.",
    "demolition": "Pakistan and Bangladesh remain stable at firm levels, with rates unchanged from last \nweek. It is important to note that Pakistan has not been tested recently, as no vessels have been sold \nthere in the past couple of months. For an overview of demolition market rates, please check our \ncomprehensive demometer below:"
  },
